  "text": {
    "markdown": "## EV vs gas car: five-year cost of ownership\n\n**Bottom line:** at 12,000 miles a year the two are almost identical after five years. The gas car is ahead by just **$100**. The EV breaks even about one month into year six and is cheaper every year after that.\n\n| | EV | Gas car |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Purchase price | $38,000 | $30,000 |\n| Energy or fuel per year (12,000 mi) | $480 | $1,560 |\n| Maintenance per year | $400 | $900 |\n| **Running cost per year** | **$880** | **$2,460** |\n| Running cost over 5 years | $4,400 | $12,300 |\n| **Total after 5 years** | **$42,400** | **$42,300** |\n\n### How it adds up\n\n- **EV:** 12,000 mi × $0.04 = $480 energy, plus $400 maintenance = $880 a year. Over five years: $38,000 + 5 × $880 = **$42,400**.\n- **Gas:** 12,000 mi × $0.13 = $1,560 fuel, plus $900 maintenance = $2,460 a year. Over five years: $30,000 + 5 × $2,460 = **$42,300**.\n\nThe EV costs $8,000 more up front and saves $1,580 a year to run, so it needs 8,000 ÷ 1,580 ≈ **5.1 years** (about 60,800 miles) to catch up.\n\n### Year by year\n\n| Year | EV total | Gas total | Cheaper so far |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n| 1 | $38,880 | $32,460 | Gas by $6,420 |\n| 2 | $39,760 | $34,920 | Gas by $4,840 |\n| 3 | $40,640 | $37,380 | Gas by $3,260 |\n| 4 | $41,520 | $39,840 | Gas by $1,680 |\n| 5 | $42,400 | $42,300 | Gas by $100 |\n| 6 | $43,280 | $44,760 | EV by $1,480 |\n| 8 | $45,040 | $49,680 | EV by $4,640 |\n\n### What would tip it\n\n- **Drive more and the EV wins sooner.** At 15,000 miles a year the EV saves $1,850 a year and is ahead by $1,250 at five years.\n- **Keep the car longer.** Every extra year adds $1,580 to the EV's lead.\n- **Not included here:** resale value, incentives or tax credits, insurance, home charger installation and financing. Any of these can be larger than the $100 gap, so check them for your situation.\n",
    "validation": {
      "valid": true,
      "checks": [
        "is non-empty Markdown",
        "contains no raw HTML outside code (react-markdown would print it literally)"
      ],
      "errors": [],
      "warnings": []
    }
  },
